Date: Sat, 10 Oct 2026 21:08:53 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 78/80] drm/msm/adreno: Add speed bins for A620

The downstream kgsl driver knows three A620 speed bins: 0x00 and 0x84
run up to 625 MHz, 0x73 up to 540 MHz. Map them to supported-hw bits
0, 1 and 2 so the device tree can describe the levels of each bin.

These changes were written with the help of an LLM and checked by a human.

Assisted-by: LLM dtschema
Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01RmfiVDW3KWZdb9c3iDGRYg
---
 drivers/gpu/drm/msm/adreno/a6xx_catalog.c | 5 +++++
 1 file changed, 5 insertions(+)

diff --git a/drivers/gpu/drm/msm/adreno/a6xx_catalog.c b/drivers/gpu/drm/msm/adreno/a6xx_catalog.c
index fbed96bb1..ff38f394c 100644
--- a/drivers/gpu/drm/msm/adreno/a6xx_catalog.c
+++ b/drivers/gpu/drm/msm/adreno/a6xx_catalog.c
@@ -910,6 +910,11 @@ static const struct adreno_info a6xx_gpus[] = {
 			.gmu_cgc_mode = 0x00020202,
 			.prim_fifo_threshold = 0x00010000,
 		},
+		.speedbins = ADRENO_SPEEDBINS(
+			{ 0,    0 },
+			{ 0x84, 1 },
+			{ 0x73, 2 },
+		),
 	}, {
 		.chip_ids = ADRENO_CHIP_IDS(0x06020100),
 		.family = ADRENO_6XX_GEN3,
